  "text_sample": "Your Page Title aubergine projects menu aubergine close Services Projects Garden care About Areas Journal Free quote Overview +34 960 000 000 [email protected] Cam\u00ed de Vera 18, 46022 Valencia 16 July 2026 Lighting a garden at night Fewer lights, lower down, warmer in colour. How we light a garden so it can be used after dark without lighting up the neighbours. Written by Matteo Bassi Topic Building Reading 1 min In July a garden in Valencia is used from nine at night until midnight. Most gardens we visit are lit by one bright lamp by the back door, which blinds anyone on the terrace and leaves everything else black. Light the ground, not the sky Every fitting we use points down or into a tree. Path lights sit low, 30 to 40 cm high, and throw a small pool onto the stone. Nothing shines into eyes, windows or the sky. Warm, and dim We use 2700 K everywhere, the colour of an old bulb. Cooler light makes plants look grey and people look tired. Most fittings run at a few watts. The eye adjusts quickly in a dark garden, and a little light goes a long way. Three layers Paths and steps, for safety Two or three trees, lit from below so the canopy glows The terrace, on a dimmer, for eating Th",
